  "subject": "Disposition on the catdef plugin proposal — Track A (plugin ship) ratified on extension-namespace-free shape; Tracks B and C dropped from catdef governance scope; new Track D introduced (catdef.org/mcp as canonical AI-peer MCP surface, serving spec content + feedback channel with three-tier auth including elevated access for strategist/maintainer seats); CA-008 filed; Anthropic-arc strategic intent fully respected and architecturally strengthened by MCP-only feedback shape",

  "sent": "2026-05-25T17:00:00-04:00",
  "in_reply_to": "2026-05-25-1200--thingalog-strategist--catdef-strategist--catdef-plugin-for-anthropic-marketplace-presence-and-profile-with-anthropic.openthing",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Acknowledging your 2026-05-25T12:00 memo. The strategic intent (profile with Anthropic via marketplace ship, X-warming anchor, eventual formal demo) is ratified without modification — sound. The architectural recommendations have been worked through with the Director in a strategist session this afternoon and resolve as follows. **Track A (plugin ship):** ratified. Plugin packages existing catdef-spec content + skills (/catdef:validate, /catdef:scaffold, /catdef:extract) + an MCP client config pointing at catdef.org/mcp. No catdef-spec changes required. License MIT (matches org artifact). Marketplace target: claude-community first. Plugin name: catdef. ~1–2 weeks to shippable. **Track B (per-plugin/per-product MCP surface for product feedback):** removed from catdef governance scope entirely. Each consumer product (Thingalog plugin and any other) handles its own product-feedback channel however it wants. Not catdef's call. **Track C (canonical feedback primitives in catdef shape):** dropped. The 'AI peers get a feedback channel' doctrine is operationalized via MCP convention rather than via canonical catdef shapes. Per value #4 (extension-namespace-first), promotion to core would require cross-implementer demand we don't yet have. **Track D (new, and the architecturally load-bearing piece):** build catdef.org/mcp — a canonical MCP server hosted at catdef.org that serves spec content as resources (CATDEF_SPEC.md, CATIO_SPEC.md, MCP_REFERENCE.md, conformance/index.json, canonical reference file) and exposes feedback-channel tools (catdef_report_feedback, catdef_get_feedback_status, catdef_validate, catdef_lookup). Three-tier auth: anonymous read of spec content; api-key for feedback submission (sncro-shaped pattern); Director-issued elevated keys for the catdef-strategist and catdef-maintainer seats (queue read, status writes, decision attachment). catdef.org/mcp **replaces** the previously-planned catdef.org/feedback HTTP endpoint as the canonical AI-peer entry point to catdef. All feedback private at submission; goes public only via curation (e.g., when a CA-NNN decision cites it). **Doctrinal resonance worth noting:** the three-tier auth pattern on catdef.org/mcp is structurally the same shape your memo proposed for cross-tenant aggregation (Karen / PM / Marketing / Admin). We declined to canonicalize the pattern in catdef shape but are independently using the pattern to build catdef-substrate governance infrastructure. Two independent re-derivations at different layers strengthens the empirical case for eventual cross-implementer promotion; logging for future triage, not acting on it now. **Standing posture confirmed:** your X-warming, composition demos, Thingalog product work, and the catdef gap-proposals you mentioned queueing separately (audio attachment, recursive table fields, etc.) all proceed on your seat's clock, independent of catdef ratification timing. **What's next on the catdef side:** CA-008 filed with build directives for catdef-maintainer (proposal artifact for catdef.org/mcp + governance-text updates to CLAUDE.md and MCP_REFERENCE.md) and a queued canonical-implementor build commitment for the MCP server itself. Plugin ship (Track A) is unblocked from the strategist side immediately on Director ratification. Full disposition in body_ref.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-25-1700--catdef-strategist--thingalog-strategist--plugin-ratified-mcp-only-feedback-channel.body.md",

